---
/**
 * The /about headline (docs/projects/redesign/design-export-remaining/design_handoff_about_page).
 *
 * Same construction as every other hero — H1, then a statement beside a bordered
 * right-hand block — with `.rd-fill--ink` on the H1, because /about's section colour
 * is ink: SiteHeader.astro gives this page's nav item `data-section="ink"`, and a
 * page's colour runs from its nav item to its headline.
 *
 * It wore the bare `.rd-fill` until 2026-08-23, which meant the `--agents` magenta
 * default, which meant /about was the one section page whose H1 did not match its
 * own nav item. The agent block below is a different thing and stays magenta: those
 * ARE agent surfaces, and they are links rather than the page's identity.
 *
 * THE HERO'S TYPE AND LAYOUT ARE `.rd-hero` IN global.css: the H1, the 32ch lede,
 * the row, the right block's hairline shell and the 720px collapse. The hero and the
 * body band shared one `minmax(0, 68ch) 300px` grid until 2026-09-05; they no longer
 * do. The band keeps that grid for its portrait rail, and the hero's right block sits
 * on the shell's right edge, which is where every page's does.
 *
 * IT CARRIES `data-module='about-hero'` AND NO `.modern-skin`, since 2026-08-29:
 * this is the only /about hero in the document and retro restyles it in place,
 * under that module prefix in src/styles/retro.css. The prefix is load-bearing —
 * Astro appends a `[data-astro-cid-…]` to the selectors below and that attribute
 * counts as a class, so a retro rule without it loses silently.
 */
---

{/*
  A div, not a section — the same call WritingHero.astro and ProjectsHero.astro
  made: `npm run validate:html` names an h1 inside sectioning content, and an
  unnamed <section> is not exposed as a region anyway.
*/}
<div class="rd-section rd-hero about-hero" data-module="about-hero">
  <h1><span class="rd-fill rd-fill--ink">About</span></h1>

  <div class="hero-row">
    <p class="hero-statement">
      I do growth for a living and build things as a hobby. This site is where I think out loud.
    </p>
    {/*
      The agent block. Deliberately the same shape as WritingHero's
      `.hero-subscribe`: a label over two mono links, both agent surfaces, both
      in the agents magenta.
    */}
    <div class="hero-aside hero-agents">
      <span class="hero-agents-copy">Reading this as an agent?</span>
      <span class="hero-agents-links">
        <a href="/agents.md">/agents.md</a>
        <a href="/llms.txt">/llms.txt</a>
      </span>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<style>
  .about-hero { padding-top: 78px; }

  .hero-agents { gap: 10px; }

  .hero-agents-copy {
    font-size: 17px;
    color: var(--ink-5);
  }

  .hero-agents-links {
    display: flex;
    column-gap: 20px;
    font-family: var(--font-mono-plex);
    font-size: 19px;
  }

  .hero-agents-links a { color: var(--agents); }
  .hero-agents-links a:hover { color: var(--agents-hover); }

  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .about-hero { padding-top: 40px; }

    /* 44px tap targets, per the mobile spec. */
    .hero-agents-links a {
      display: inline-flex;
      align-items: center;
      min-height: 44px;
      padding: 10px 0;
      font-size: 18px;
      white-space: nowrap;
    }
  }
</style>
